  "live_records": {
    "q-37950": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37950",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate the repeated integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡y}[{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡y}[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x]_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡y}(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡y}(-(-1)+0)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{tan}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡0 \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
