    "q-37931": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37931",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{7\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{\\pi }^{7\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+y)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+y)]}_{\\pi }^{7\\pi /6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{3}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi +y))\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{3}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi +y))\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{3}+y)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi +y)]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{3}+0)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi +0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{17\\pi }{6})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}+0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
