    "q-72050": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72050",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}{[\\frac{\\,{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{2}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}(\\frac{256}{4}-\\frac{16}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}60{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}60{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =60{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =60\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
