    "q-73594": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73594",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,-2\\le y\\le -1\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:        \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}9{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}9{y}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{2}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}9{y}^{2}(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}9{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}21{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}21{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =21{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =21(\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
