    "q-72198": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72198",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{x}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{y}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{y}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y[{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)]_{1}^{e}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
